e?","options":["The signum function records every decimal digit of $x$.","The signum function is only defined for integers.","Numbers with the same sign can have the same signum value even if their magnitudes differ.","The signum function changes unordered collections into sequences, regardless of the specific input chosen."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"308ce5e2cc711187874b2e29"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_signum_function_5799e175_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How does the signum function reflect trichotomy of real numbers?","options":["It makes every real number positive.","It proves every real number is rational, no matter which values are selected.","It removes the zero case.","It separates inputs into positive, zero, and negative cases."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"72594611ff7697f0d76d5713"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_signum_function_5799e175_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which statement correctly evaluates both values?","options":["$\\mathrm{sgn}(5) = -1$ and $\\mathrm{sgn}(-5) = 1$","$\\mathrm{sgn}(5) = 0$ and $\\mathrm{sgn}(-5) = 0$","$\\mathrm{sgn}(5) = 5$ and $\\mathrm{sgn}(-5) = -5$","$\\mathrm{sgn}(5) = 1$ and $\\mathrm{sgn}(-5) = -1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6b090cf5f7c12db805676560"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_signum_function_5799e175_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which input is the boundary case in the piecewise definition of $\\mathrm{sgn}$?","options":["$x = 2$","$x = 0$","$x = -2$","$x = 1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7c6e8e25ef33254ad096b74e"},{"id":"signum_function_new_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which identity relates $x$, $\\mathrm{sgn}(x)$, and $|x|$?","options":["$x=\\mathrm{sgn}(x)\\,|x|$","$x=\\mathrm{sgn}(x)+|x|$","$|x|=\\mathrm{sgn}(x)$","$x=|x|$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revisi